    "recap": {
      "id": "recap",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "When powers are added or subtracted, do not add or subtract their exponents directly.\n\n1. Pick the smaller common power.\n2. Factor it out.\n3. Simplify the ordinary bracket.\n4. Rewrite to a common base and solve.\n\nExplain why 2^x + 2^(x+1) becomes 3×2^x, not 2^(2x+1).",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
